{
 "schema": "pee.property-definitions.v1",
 "version": "pd.1",
 "statement": "Declarative definitions of observable properties (I-ADOPT: property + object of interest + constraints; VIM: measurand vs influence quantity; LOINC: basis/time aspect as identity). One definition is consumed by reading (plan), interpretation (contract slots), attribution (which property a value reports) and evaluation (which conditions decide comparability). Properties and condition dimensions are shared across product categories; a category profile only says which properties apply and which conditions DEFINE the measurand there. Quantity kinds, metrics and units come from the quantity-knowledge pack. Written in PEE's own words; no third-party text reproduced. Every entry carries a lifecycle state (candidate | supported | verified | decision_usable) and its sources. A condition may define the measurand only for one basis (onlyForBasis): the usage pattern defines a periodic figure, not a per-run one.",
